### Presigned API HTTP Requests
### Use with RestClient VS Code extension or Postman

@baseUrl = https://localhost:5001
@objectKey = videos/test-video.mp4
@prefix = videos/

### Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/presignedurl/health HTTP/1.1

### Generate Download Presigned URL
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/presignedurl/download?objectKey={{objectKey}} HTTP/1.1

### Generate Upload Presigned URL
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/presignedurl/upload?objectKey={{objectKey}} HTTP/1.1

### List Objects
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/presignedurl/list?prefix={{prefix}} HTTP/1.1

### Revoke Access (Delete Object)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/presignedurl/revoke?objectKey={{objectKey}} HTTP/1.1

### Upload a File (requires a presigned URL)
# First get an upload URL from the /upload endpoint, then use that URL:
# PUT <presigned-url> < @/path/to/file.mp4

### Download a File (requires a presigned URL)
# First get a download URL from the /download endpoint, then:
# GET <presigned-url>
